格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Mnemosyne 记忆层在 DeepSeek Harness 中的插件 — 本地优先、SQLite 支持的跨会话记忆。","id":"gh:1342777533","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-mnemosyne","slug":"rebron1900/dsh-mnemosyne","topics":["ai-memory","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","memory","mnemosyne"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Mnemosyne 记忆层在 DeepSeek Harness 中的插件 — 本地优先、SQLite 支持的跨会话记忆。"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-mnemosyne"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"> A DeepSeek Harness plugin for Mnemosyne — local-first, SQLite-backed cross-session memory."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"> Local-first memory for DSH: remember, recall, and consolidate context across sessions."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## About Mnemosyne"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Mnemosyne is a zero-cloud, SQLite-backed, local-first AI memory system. One `pip install`, one SQLit"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"e file, no external services required. It uses a **BEAM** (Bilevel Episodic-Associative Memory) arch"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"o external services required. It uses a **BEAM** (Bilevel Episodic-Associative Memory) architecture:"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"- **Working Memory** — Hot context tier, auto-injected before LLM calls, TTL-based eviction\n- **Epis"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"odic Memory** — Long-term storage with sqlite-vec + FTS5 hybrid search (50% vector similarity + 30% "},{"id":"p8s3","text":"FTS5 rank + 20% importance)\n- **TripleStore** — Temporal knowledge graph with version chains"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Mnemosyne supports MCP, Python SDK, and multiple agent frameworks (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, OpenW"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"ebUI, Pi, etc.). This plugin integrates it into DSH."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## About Pi-mnemosyne"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"This plugin is ported from `@mnemosyne-oss/pi-mnemosyne` — the official Pi coding agent extension fo"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"r Mnemosyne. All memory logic lives in the `mnemosyne` CLI (`pip install mnemosyne-memory`), and the"},{"id":"p11s3","text":" plugin stays CLI-first: normal shared-memory operations shell out to the CLI. The port to DSH adds "},{"id":"p11s4","text":"a settings panel, automatic CLI installation, config management, turn-end auto-consolidation, and — "},{"id":"p11s5","text":"beyond the original stateless proxy — a few thin bridges that do not reimplement memory logic: a sma"},{"id":"p11s6","text":"ll Python helper run through the CLI's venv interpreter for session-scoped access, direct-SQLite sco"},{"id":"p11s7","text":"pe migrations, and an env bridge for the write filter (`ignore_patterns` / `write_classifier`)."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"- **Six native tools**: `mnemosyne_remember` / `mnemosyne_recall` / `mnemosyne_forget` / `mnemosyne_"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"stats` / `mnemosyne_sleep` / `mnemosyne_bind`\n- **Filtered memory management**: In the Memory browse"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"r, filter the list, select individual records or all records currently shown, then batch-edit trust,"},{"id":"p13s4","text":" expiry, importance, lifecycle status, or scope. Workspace bindings remain available as batch move t"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"argets; no content is overwritten.\n- **Embedded skill**: The `mnemosyne` skill auto-registers with t"},{"id":"p13s6","text":"he plugin, guiding agents on when to store/retrieve memories\n- **Settings panel**: A dedicated \"Mnem"},{"id":"p13s7","text":"osyne\" entry in DSH Settings with CLI status, memory stats, one-click install/test, and a config for"},{"id":"p13s8","text":"m\n- **Memory dashboard**: Opens from the Mnemosyne Settings panel through the optional Better Sideba"},{"id":"p13s9","text":"r integration, showing the active bank's overview, memory browser, filtered batch management, triple"},{"id":"p13s10","text":"s, consolidation history, search, and detail views. Management actions are explicit and confirmed.\n-"},{"id":"p13s11","text":" **Auto-install CLI**: The panel's Setup button runs `uv tool install mnemosyne-memory` and fills `c"},{"id":"p13s12","text":"onfig.yaml` defaults\n- **Data isolation**: SQLite DB and `config.yaml` live under `~/.dsh/mnemosyne`"},{"id":"p13s13","text":", never touching `~/.hermes`\n- **Config sync**: The panel reads actual values from the flat `config."},{"id":"p13s14","text":"yaml`; empty fields show default placeholders; saving triggers `mnemosyne config reload`\n- **Reset t"},{"id":"p13s15","text":"o defaults**: The panel footer resets all managed config keys to Mnemosyne upstream defaults\n- **Aut"},{"id":"p13s16","text":"o-consolidation**: Queues memory work per session; every 10 durable turns checks working-memory coun"},{"id":"p13s17","text":"t and runs `mnemosyne sleep` for the current session when the threshold is met. A cleared `sleep_thr"},{"id":"p13s18","text":"eshold` falls back to the upstream default (50) — never 0 — and `session/disposed` only forces a fin"},{"id":"p13s19","text":"al consolidation when that session actually stored automatic memories, so idle sessions never trigge"},{"id":"p13s20","text":"r an LLM-backed sleep\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Installation"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Install from GitHub (without npm)"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"> The Setup button requires `uv` on PATH. If you don't have uv yet:\n>\n[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Configuration"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Configuration comes from two sources: the plugin's own DSH settings (`~/.dsh/settings.yaml` under th"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"e `mnemosyne:` namespace) and Mnemosyne's flat `~/.dsh/mnemosyne/config.yaml`. The panel shows confi"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"g.yaml values first; missing values display default placeholders."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"| Group | Fields | Source |"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"| Plugin | `cli` / `defaultTopK` / `timeoutMs` / `dataDir` | DSH settings / `cordis.patch.yml` |\n| E"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"mbedding | `noEmbeddings` / `embeddingModel` / `embeddingDim` / `embeddingApiUrl` / `embeddingApiKey"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"` | config.yaml `no_embeddings` / `embedding_*` |\n| LLM | `llmEnabled` / `llmBaseUrl` / `llmApiKey` "},{"id":"p22s4","text":"/ `llmModel` / `llmTimeout` | config.yaml `llm_*` |\n| Recall | `polyphonicRecall` | config.yaml `pol"},{"id":"p22s5","text":"yphonic_recall` |\n| Working Memory | `wmMaxItems` / `wmTtlHours` | config.yaml `wm_*` |\n| Working Me"},{"id":"p22s6","text":"mory | `autoSleep` / `sleepThreshold` / `ignorePatterns` / `syncRoles` | config.yaml `auto_sleep_ena"},{"id":"p22s7","text":"bled` / `sleep_threshold` / `ignore_patterns` / `sync_roles` |\n| Automatic Memory | `promptSection` "},{"id":"p22s8","text":"/ `autoSync` / `syncTurnUserLimit` / `syncTurnAssistantLimit` / `autoPrefetch` / `recallMode` / `aut"},{"id":"p22s9","text":"oWriteScope` / `prefetchTopK` / `prefetchMinQueryLen` | DSH settings / `cordis.patch.yml` |"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"> **Note**: The Automatic Memory fields are DSH-side config (saved via the Settings panel, not writt"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"en to `config.yaml`). They take effect at runtime via the settings watcher — no DSH restart needed."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"The plugin stays CLI-first: shared-memory operations use the `mnemosyne` CLI, while session-scoped o"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"perations use a small Python helper through the CLI's venv interpreter. No memory logic is reimpleme"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"nted in Node. It is no longer a *pure* stateless proxy, though, because the migration route writes S"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"QLite scope metadata directly and the write-filter env bridge reads `config.yaml` on every call."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## Design Document"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"See docs/design.md."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"## Development"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
